---
import PostCard from "@/components/PostCard.astro";
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import { getLatestPosts } from "@/sanity/queries/posts";
const posts = await getLatestPosts();
---

<Layout>
  <div class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-8">
    <div
      class="flex w-full flex-col items-center gap-2 text-justify leading-relaxed tracking-tight lg:w-1/2"
    >
      <p>
        Every story ever told is an echo of another. A whisper passed between
        worlds, a thread pulled from one reality and woven into the next. Echoes
        is a collection of those threads — stories set across a loose multiverse
        of worlds that brush against each other, share their myths, and
        sometimes bleed into one another in ways their inhabitants would never
        expect.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some of these worlds are ancient, ruled by gods who have long since
        grown tired of their own names. Others are quieter — small towns,
        cramped apartments, ordinary lives interrupted by the extraordinary.
        There are places where magic is a trade and places where it is a wound.
        Heroes who do not know they are heroes, and villains who believe, with
        complete sincerity, that they are not.
      </p>
      <p>
        You do not need to read everything to find your footing here. Each story
        stands on its own. But the longer you stay, the more familiar certain
        shadows will become — a name overheard in a tavern that appears again in
        a letter found three worlds away, a constellation that means something
        different depending on who is looking up. The multiverse rewards the
        curious.
      </p>
      <p>Start anywhere. The echoes will find you.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex w-full flex-col items-center">
      <h3 class="mb-2">Latest Stories</h3>
      <ul class="flex w-full flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
        {
          posts.map((post) => (
            <li class="w-full">
              <PostCard
                post={post}
                type={
                  post.category.title === "One Shot"
                    ? `one-shots`
                    : post.series
                      ? `series/${post.series.slug.current}`
                      : "/"
                }
              />
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
